			},
			"moralist": {
				"type": "score",
				"instructions": "`chapter` is a passage of a novel of some 3,000 words. Read it as a critic of the moral tradition would: one who asks whether it tells the truth about how people live and what they owe each other, and whether it enlarges the reader's sympathy, and cares little for technique for its own sake. What is it to such a critic?",
